enum StatisticID {
    None
    SourceFilesChecked SourceFilesInferred SourceFilesTypesOnly SourceFilesData SourceFilesRuntime SourceFilesDemoted SourceBytes SourceLines
    SourceBytesOfPackages SourceLinesOfPackages SourceBytesOfDeclarations SourceLinesOfDeclarations SourceBytesOfBun SourceLinesOfBun
    FunctionsLowered ValuesLowered ProgramBytes
    # The functions that the front end knows by their text as helpers that a compiler or a bundler publishes, and the calls of such helpers in whose place it wrote out what they do.
    KnownHelperFunctions KnownHelperCalls
    # Of the table of modules of the link: CommonJS modules without an exports object (a variable for each name), those with one variable for `module.exports`, and the records that a CommonJS file has beside its own for ES importers.
    ModulesWithNames ModulesWithValue Faces
    # The pairs of a layout and a name for which Link gives the layout a field that the front end does not list.
    FlowAppendedFields
    # What the plan decides. Modules that keep no status . sites that require a module by calling its code . RecordRequire operations that stay . async functions in which nothing suspends . fields in the extension of their object . functions that hand back a number or undefined raw.
    ModulesWithoutState RequireSitesBound RequiresRecorded AsyncWorkersMade FieldsOutOfLine NumbersOrUndefinedReturnedRaw
    # What the walk builds: Walker::count(). It counts what is walked: a body at each call that it is read at.
    URLsLeftUnbuilt IteratorsSteppedWithoutCall SerializersCreated OwnKeyWalksExpanded
    # Calls of a built-in in whose place a function of the library is called directly or copied . of those, sorts by a function that calls no comparator . ArraySpeciesCreate built as a new list . closures made in front of the last call of a copy alone.
    LibraryFunctionsEnteredBehindRows SortsThatCallNoComparator NewListsInPlaceOfSpecies ClosuresMadeWhereCopiesHandThemOn
    # Only where the access counts are asked for, which --explain=statistics does. The written places that read, store, define, ask for or delete a property, by what the code that is left there knows . the records that are kept in a form that holds a double.
    AccessesProven AccessesGuarded AccessesUnknown ValuesInDouble
    # What the emitters and the machine make.
    NativeFunctionsCalledDirectly NativeFunctionTestsEmitted ExactIntegersBehindNumbers StepsThatKnowTheDeletedPrefix LoopsRotated
    InnerPointersAcrossSafepoints NullChecksFoldedIntoAccesses
    # Of the image.
    InlineFramesEmitted FrameMapBytesEmitted RegExpCandidatesCompiled
    # Counted by nothing yet: what each of them counted in an earlier compiler has no counterpart here. A stored program asks for it with `Todo:` behind its bound, which fails the day it is counted.
    EnvironmentsPromotedToVariables UnreadVariableStoresRemoved LiteralArgumentsTakenApart GetsAnsweredByHas SlotStoreRunGroups KeyPartsLookupGroups
    StoresLeftInLoopsForOthers ElementPresenceTestsPlaced ArrayChainsFused ArrayCapacitiesPlanned AllocationsSunk SwitchesTestedByWindow
    InitializersDeferred ClosuresDeferredInVariables ClassesDeferredInVariables FlowListsNeverToldApart RestartsInGenericVersion
    TagLookupsWithOtherKeys ObjectKeysSearchedInLine BirthsFinished
    TypesInterned
    FunctionsRead ValuesRead
    ValuesScanned FactNodes FactEdges FactsCarriedOverEdges FactRounds FactRuleCalls
    UnitsCompiled UnitsWrittenStraight ValuesWalked ValuesWalkedAndKept LoopsWalkedAgain CallsInlined OperationsBuilt OperationsSwept OperationsEmitted
    MachineOperationsAppended MachineOperationsScanned MachineOperationsAllocated MachineOperationsEncoded ValuesSpilled
    FormsThatDifferFromSchema FormsPickedByPlaceOtherThanLoop
    DirectCalls IndirectCalls TestsThatRejoin LoopsBuiltTwice TurnsThatBeginAgain
    AssignmentsWrittenOutFieldByField JoinsWalkedOnceForEachWay
    # TestingSwitch::CheckProofsAtRunTime: the CheckProof operations that were built, by ProofSource, and the values whose proven type says more than any test can tell.
    ProofsCheckedOfEntryParameters ProofsCheckedOfResultsOfCalls ProofsCheckedOfFields ProofsCheckedOfVariables ProofsCheckedOfCaptures ProofsCheckedOfContents ProofsCheckedOfCallees ProofsCheckedOfOtherOperations ProofsCheckedOfTests ProofsCheckedOfWhatIsRemembered
    ProofsThatNoTestTells
    FunctionsWithAllIndirectCallersListed GenericEntriesOpenedByIndirectCalls GenericEntriesOpenedBesideCompiledTarget ClosedGenericEntries
    IndirectCallsThatMayEnterAnyClosure
    OffsetsFoundByComparisons OffsetsFoundInFlatTables OffsetsFoundInHashedTables OffsetsFoundInPagedTables BytesOfFlatOffsetTables BytesOfHashedOffsetTables BytesOfPagedOffsetTables
    ThingsMentioned ThingsNumbered IdentifiersNumbered StringConstantsNumbered NamesWithoutColumn MethodTableSelectors MethodTableBytes
    ClassGuardCounts GuardsOfClassGuardCounts
    ImageFunctionsEmitted CodeBytesEmitted StubBytes ConstantBytesEmitted TableBytesEmitted TextBytesEmitted Veneers StubCopiesEmitted
    RegExpsCompiled RegExpsInterpreted
    WasmFunctionsCompiled WasmFunctionsWithTwoCopies WasmCodeBytesEmitted WasmCodeBytesOfSecondCopies
    FunctionBytesEmitted FarInstanceWordBytesEmitted VeneerBytesEmitted SharedCodeBytesEmitted ArgumentThunkBytes PaddingBytesBetweenFunctions
    FinalJumpBytesRemoved
    FFICodeBytesEmitted FFIDirectoryBytesEmitted RegExpCodeBytesEmitted RegExp16BitCodeBytes RegExpTableBytesEmitted PaddingBytesBetweenCodeParts
    ConstantBytesOfSharedConstants ConstantBytesOfShapeSets ConstantBytesOfBitSetsOverKnownShapes ConstantBytesOfOffsetTables ConstantBytesOfCellTemplates ConstantBytesOfNumbers
    UnlabeledConstantBytes ConstantBytesOfJumpTables PaddingBytesBetweenConstants
    # The units of parsers that are written out of types. An outside build script fails a build that does not report the name with 0.
    ParsersCreated
    # The same script wants each of these four with 0, which --aot-harden=proof-checks,ignore-told-ranges brings about. The names are those of the compiler that the script was written for.
    # AllocateInFramesChanges: the cells that are emitted into frames and the layouts of scopes whose cells the plan hands back (Mechanism::CellsInFrames). ClosuresInFrames: the closures among the first.
    # RangeChecksRemoved: the accesses by position that are emitted without a test of the position. KnownInductionsUsed: the pointers into storage and the lengths that a read in a loop takes from in front of the loop.
    AllocateInFramesChanges ClosuresInFrames RangeChecksRemoved KnownInductionsUsed
    # The calls that are built to parse by a written type. The same script prints the name.
    TypedResultsSelected
    # The calls of Array.prototype.slice that are a list of elements which the walk had in sight.
    SlicesMadeOfElementsInSight
    VectorsOfViewsRead
    AccessesInsideViews
}
extend StatisticID with Stage suffix Nanoseconds as time

enum RuntimeCounterID {
    None
    FieldsLeftSlotByDelete FieldsLeftSlotByRedefinition FieldsLeftSlotByStoreOfOtherType KeyOrdersStoredOutOfLine
    ObjectsGivenIntegrityLevel ObjectsLaidBelowOtherPrototype ClassGuardBitsEnded MethodTableMadeWritable
    FieldMovePlansMade AssignmentPlansMade CopiesCollectedByName CopiesByOrdinaryLookups
    CompiledStructuresMade
    StarsRecorded StarsCarriedOutLate
    CompiledModulesWalkedByLoader FilesComparedWithDisk
    SiteCacheRefills
    JSONStringifySlowPaths StringBuilderGrowths RegExpsCreatedWithoutRecord
    TextsParsedByOwnParser ObjectsParsedIntoRecords ObjectsParsedIntoOrdinaryObjects
    RegExpPatternsParsed RegExpsCompiledToBytecode RegExpMatchesInterpreted
    RegExpsPreparedForLongSearches RegExpLongSearchesHandedOver RegExpWideSubjectsRefused RegExpSubjectsNarrowed
    RegExpLiteralsCompiledToBytecode RegExpPredictedTextsCompiledToBytecode RegExpImageCodeGaveUp
    RegExpPredictedTextsCreated RegExpPredictedTextsGivenCode RegExpLiteralsGivenCode
    InterpretedGlobalCode InterpretedEvalCode InterpretedFunctionCode InterpretedModuleCode
    DirectEvalsParsed
    StackListingsAfterGivenUpCaptures
    ModulesForRequireCache ModulesForWhatHasRun LinksBelowRoots StacksOfThrows RunsBelowListedFrames
    ReadsOffNoCellThatFaulted
    GraphsHeldBehindEarlierCalls GraphsLetGoBehindEarlierCalls
}
